Package: singlet
Type: Package
Title: Access the Singlet Single-Cell Atlas
Version: 1.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zach", "DeBruine", email = "zacharydebruine@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates", role = "cph",
           comment = "Zstandard library bundled in src/zstd"),
    person("Yann", "Collet", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Zstandard and xxHash, bundled in src/zstd"))
Description: Load, search and analyze the Singlet single-cell RNA sequencing
    atlas <https://singlet.bio> from R. Public studies from the Gene Expression
    Omnibus are reprocessed from raw reads with one pipeline and published as
    one '.s1' object per sample, listed by a manifest per study. The package
    reads the manifests, fetches only the parts of the sample objects it needs
    by HTTP range requests, caches them, and assembles count matrices, per-cell
    labels (cell type, chromosomal sex, genetic ancestry) and quality-control
    metrics into 'SingleCellExperiment' or 'Seurat' objects. It also searches
    the atlas for studies or for cells by their labels and sample metadata.
    Sparse count matrices are decoded by a header-only C++ reader shared with
    the Singlet 'Python' package, using the bundled 'Zstandard' library.
